It's specificially notable, that many rafsi are the same as cmavo. I think all 
do, except for the ones ending in a consonant. Those would be seen as cmevla, 
but I personally believe, that a big part of the fun of listening to a song, 
that has "garbled" or "weird" or even especially poetical lyrics is to find out 
what the author intended to mean.
There might even be the possibility to make lyrics make sense when words are 
interpreted as being cmavo and when they are interpreted as rafsi standing for 
gismu.
The possibilities are endless :)
